.TH INSTALL-CLAUDE-SKILLS.SH 1 "2026-09-28" "requests-fermi-sso 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
install-claude-skills.sh, install-claude-skills.ps1 \- install Claude Code skills
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./install-claude-skills.sh
.RB [ \-t
.IR DIR ]...
.RB [ \-a ]
.RB [ \-l ]
.RB [ \-u ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.br
.B .\einstall-claude-skills.ps1
.RB [ \-Target
.IR DIR [, DIR ...]]
.RB [ \-All ]
.RB [ \-Link ]
.RB [ \-Uninstall ]
.RB [ \-Force ]
.RB [ \-DryRun ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installs the Claude Code skills shipped in
.I claude-skills/
at user level, so every Claude Code session that uses the target config
directory sees them, whatever project it is started in.
.PP
The skills are:
.TP
.B fermi-sso
Running
.BR fermi-sso-probe (1),
.BR fermi-sso-cookies (1)
and
.B fermi-sso-yubikey
to log in to Fermilab SSO, check or reuse a cookie jar, and diagnose failures.
.TP
.B fermi-sso-embed
Adding
.BR FermiSSOSession (3)
to another project: pinned dependency, configuration, success checks,
threading, offline tests.
.PP
Each skill directory
.IR claude-skills/NAME/
is placed at
.IR DIR/skills/NAME/ .
A config directory is shared by every settings profile that uses it (for
example several
.I settings-*.json
files in
.IR ~/.claude ),
so one install covers all of them. Separate config directories selected
with
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
each need their own install; use
.BR \-a .
.PP
A copied skill carries a
.I .installed-from-requests-fermi-sso
marker; a linked one is a symlink (a junction on Windows). Only skills
with one of those are replaced or removed without
.BR \-f ,
so a hand-edited skill of the same name is not lost silently. Re-running
updates the installed copies in place.
.PP
The Windows script takes the same options in PowerShell form and behaves
the same way.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target " \fIDIR\fR"
Claude config directory to install into. Repeatable. Default:
.B $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
if set, else
.IR ~/.claude .
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Also install into every Claude Code config directory found:
.IR ~/.claude ,
each
.IR ~/.claude\-* ,
and
.BR $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR .
A directory qualifies if it holds
.IR settings.json ,
.IR projects/ ,
.IR skills/ ,
.IR CLAUDE.md ,
.I sessions/
or
.IR plugins/ ;
others are reported as skipped and can be named with
.BR \-t .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-link
Symlink instead of copying, so edits in the checkout take effect
immediately. Links point at this checkout; do not use it from a worktree
or checkout you plan to delete.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-uninstall
Remove the skills.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Replace or remove a same-named skill that this script did not install.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print what would be done and change nothing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Default target when no
.B \-t
is given; also included by
.BR \-a .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&./install-claude-skills.sh                  # ~/.claude
\&./install-claude-skills.sh \-a \-n            # preview every config dir
\&./install-claude-skills.sh \-a               # install everywhere
\&./install-claude-skills.sh \-l               # symlink, for skill development
\&./install-claude-skills.sh \-t ~/.claude\-personal
\&./install-claude-skills.sh \-a \-u            # remove everywhere
.fi
.PP
Windows:
.nf
powershell \-ExecutionPolicy Bypass \-File .\einstall-claude-skills.ps1 \-All
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if
.I claude-skills/
is missing, 2 on a usage error. A skill that is kept rather than
replaced is reported, not treated as an error.
.SH NOTES
Claude Code picks up new or changed user-level skills without a restart.
The claude.ai web and desktop apps do not read these directories; upload
a skill there as a zip of its directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fermi-sso-probe (1),
.BR fermi-sso-cookies (1),
.BR FermiSSOSession (3),
.BR fermi_sso_yubikey (3),
.BR bootstrap.sh (1)
